# This repo is public GitHub

`kvietmeier/Terraform` is a **stripped-down example library** for customers, colleagues, and a live CV — not a dump of lab/project state.

## Do

- Ship teachable stacks with placeholder IPs/domains/hostnames
- Commit `*.auto.tfvars.example` / `*.tfvars.example` only
- Keep real tfvars gitignored; sync privately via `scripts/sync-tfvars-personal.sh` → `~/github/personal/terraform-tfvars/`
- Document auth with `TF_VAR_*` placeholders, not private `set_var*` helpers
- Keep generic provider examples (including `vastdata/` patterns) if they teach with placeholders

## Do not commit

- Real `*.tfvars` / `*.auto.tfvars`
- `*.tfstate`, `*.tfstate.*`, `.terraform/`, `.terraform.lock.hcl`
- Internal hosts (`var54`, inventory names), org account/SSO IDs, IT tickets with live evidence
- Personal domains, passwords, private notes paths, customer-specific VIP/SG lists
- Project-specific VAST lab state (real clusters, VIP lists, customer configs) — examples only under `vastdata/`

## Where project-specific work goes

| Destination | Path |
|-------------|------|
| Internal GitLab | `~/gitlab/` (e.g. `vastoncloud/`, `sre-runbooks/`, cloud lab trees) |
| Personal tfvars mirror | `~/github/personal/terraform-tfvars/` |

Never “just this once” into this public repo.

When scrubbing for publish, follow the personal skill `public-private-git-split`.
